IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-art1-defined-terms`
IMPORT `g7-interpretation`
IMPORT `g7-vintages`
IMPORT `g7-commencement`
IMPORT `g9-common`
IMPORT `g9-interpretation`
IMPORT `g9-sched1-commissioner`
IMPORT `int-readings`
IMPORT `int-commencement`

-- int-h-text.l4: headline (e) of the integration layer: which text of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 is in force on a day, and which Parts, Articles and Schedules are in force.
-- The resolver (the nine point-in-time texts, 9.30 a.m. on 27 February 2024) is group G7's (IP2); what each text says about the Minister and the Comptroller is group G1's (IP3, Article 1);
-- the Dormant Bank Accounts words of Schedule 1 are group G9's. G1, G7 and G9 each answer the same questions from their own data; this module reads the owner's answer (G1 for the Minister and
-- the Comptroller) and the tests (int-tests-vintage-matrix.l4) assert that the three groups agree for every one of the ten values of `Vintage of the text`.
-- No Article is gated here: commencement is what this headline reports.

§ `Integration layer -- headline (e): the text of the Law and the units in force`

-- The answer for a text of the Law: everything the amendment history changes, text by text.
DECLARE `Text of the Law in force` HAS
    vintage IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc Which of the nine point-in-time texts is in force (IP2)
    `office of the Minister` IS AN `Office of the Minister` @desc The office that the definition of "Minister" in Article 1 names in that text (IP3, group G1)
    `Law that the Comptroller is defined by` IS A `Law defining the Comptroller` @desc The Law that the definition of "Comptroller" in Article 1 points at in that text (group G1)
    `paragraph (ba) is in Article 2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether sub-paragraph (ba) of Article 2(1), inserted by R&O.56/2025, is in that text (group G7's resolver; group G1 derives it from the vintage as well)
    `Schedule 1 carries the Dormant Bank Accounts words` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether paragraphs 2(4)(a) and 4(7) of Schedule 1 carry the words "subject to Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017" in that text (L.1/2017; group G9)

-- What Schedule 1 says depends on the text: with an Order under Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts Law directing the cost to the Fund, group G9's paragraph 2(4)(a) is FALSE exactly when the words are in the text.
-- This is how the integration layer reads the presence of the words from group G9 rather than from group G7's flag.
GIVEN readings IS A `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` @desc The readings of group G9
      vintage IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc The text of the Law
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Int G9 reads the Dormant Bank Accounts words in` readings vintage MEANS
    NOT (`Sch 1 para 2(4)(a) the remuneration of the Commissioner must be paid out of the annual income of the States` readings vintage TRUE)

-- The text of the Law for a vintage, every part of it computed from the owner of that part.
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet (only G7's and G9's are read here)
      vintage IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc The text of the Law
GIVETH A `Text of the Law in force`
`Int the text of the Law for the vintage` readings vintage MEANS
    `Text of the Law in force` WITH
        vintage IS vintage
        `office of the Minister` IS `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` vintage
        `Law that the Comptroller is defined by` IS `Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` vintage
        `paragraph (ba) is in Article 2(1)` IS `Endnotes: Article 2(1)(ba) is in the text of` vintage
        `Schedule 1 carries the Dormant Bank Accounts words` IS `Int G9 reads the Dormant Bank Accounts words in` (readings's `reading of Schedules 1 and 2`) vintage

-- Headline (e), by day: the text of the Law in force on the day. It refuses for a day before 1 January 2019 (no text before the first consolidated version is among the sources) and, on the
-- favoured reading of F7.1, for 27 February 2024, where the text changed at 9.30 a.m. and a question about the day alone cannot be answered.
@export Which text of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 is in force on a given day, and what that text says where the amendment history changes it: the office that "Minister" names, the Law that "Comptroller" points at, whether sub-paragraph (ba) of Article 2(1) is there, and whether Schedule 1 carries the Dormant Bank Accounts words. It refuses for a day before 1 January 2019 and for 27 February 2024 (the text changed at 9.30 a.m.; ask by instant)
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The reading taken at each fork of the nine groups (the favoured readings are `Int the favoured readings of the fleet`)
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about, for example 2026-10-02 (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A `Text of the Law in force`
`Int (e) the text of the Law in force on` readings day MEANS
    `Int the text of the Law for the vintage` readings
        (`Endnotes: the vintage of the text on` day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`))

-- Headline (e), by instant: the text in force at a moment, which is how the day of a change in the text is asked (27 February 2024 begins at 9.30 a.m. Jersey time).
@export Which text of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 is in force at a given instant (a date and time with its time zone), and what that text says where the amendment history changes it. It answers for the instant 9.30 a.m. on 27 February 2024 and for the hours either side of it; it refuses for an instant before 1 January 2019
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The reading taken at each fork of the nine groups
      moment IS A DATETIME @desc The instant asked about, with its time zone, for example 2024-02-27T09:30:00+00:00
GIVETH A `Text of the Law in force`
`Int (e) the text of the Law in force at` readings moment MEANS
    `Int the text of the Law for the vintage` readings
        (`Endnotes: the vintage of the text at` moment (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`))

-- Which units are in force on a day.
DECLARE `Units of the Law in force on a day` HAS
    `Parts in force` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc The Parts (1 to 9) that are in force, a Part brought into force in two stages counting as in force when all its Articles are
    `Articles in force` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc The Articles, as now numbered (1 to 43), that are in force
    `Schedules in force` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc The Schedules (1 and 2) that are in force

@export Which Parts, Articles (as now numbered) and Schedules of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 are in force on a given day, from the Table of Legislation History (21 November 2014, 1 May 2018, 1 January 2019). Nothing is in force before 21 November 2014
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The reading taken at each fork of the nine groups (this answer reads the commencement forks of group G7: the numbering the table speaks in, and how a Part in two stages is treated)
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about, for example 2018-05-01 (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A `Units of the Law in force on a day`
`Int (e) the units of the Law in force on` readings day MEANS
    `Units of the Law in force on a day` WITH
        `Parts in force` IS filter (GIVEN n YIELD `Commencement: the unit of the Law is in force on` (`a Part of the Law` n) day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)) (range 1 9)
        `Articles in force` IS filter (GIVEN n YIELD `Commencement: the unit of the Law is in force on` (`an Article of the Law as now numbered` n) day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)) (range 1 43)
        `Schedules in force` IS filter (GIVEN n YIELD `Commencement: the unit of the Law is in force on` (`a Schedule to the Law` n) day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)) (range 1 2)
